+### Proposed: name the steward, and route intent changes through proposals
+
+**Status**: Proposed on 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. Awaiting Justin Philpott's decision; not in force.
+**Context**: No document says who decides what this repo is for. `INTENT.md` (header) invites humans and agents to refine it, `AGENTS.md` ("Consult INTENT.md for significant decisions") tells an agent to update `INTENT.md` itself when a decision refines or challenges intent, and the local guard's check 3 says the same. None of the decisions below carries a date or a decider. The only dated statements attributed to the owner are in `explorations/` transcripts.
+**Proposal**: Justin Philpott, as repository owner, is the steward of `INTENT.md` and of the scope statements that restate it (`README.md` "Project status", `AGENTS.md` "Project Constraints"). A contributor or agent whose work would change intent records a "Proposed:" entry here instead of editing `INTENT.md`; `INTENT.md` changes only after the steward's recorded decision. New entries in this file carry a date and who decided.
+**Alternative**: keep the current practice: any contributor may revise `INTENT.md` with a dated note saying what prompted it.
+**Impact if accepted**: `AGENTS.md` "Consult INTENT.md…", the `INTENT.md` header and the local guard's intent check are reworded to match; the local guard carries the intent-change rule as drafted.
+
+---
+
+### Proposed: one guard builder, with the assessments supplying its checks
+
+**Status**: Proposed on 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. Awaiting Justin Philpott's decision; not in force.
+**Context**: Two skills build session-end guards, with different templates: `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 and `session-coherence-skill-generator`. `INTENT.md` ("The guard lifecycle: four distinct tools") names only `entropy-assessment` and `docs-first-planning-assessment` as the generator; `README.md` and `AGENTS.md` list `session-coherence-skill-generator` as a generator of session handoff guards. No skill routes to `session-coherence-skill-generator`, and `guards-integrator` still expects `entropy-assessment` to generate guards, which it no longer does (see "Specialize first around docs-first planning repos…").
+**Proposal**: `session-coherence-skill-generator` becomes the only skill that writes guards. `docs-first-planning-assessment` keeps its analysis and supplies its docs-first checks to it; `entropy-assessment` routes young repos to its bootstrap mode; `guards-integrator` takes its input from it.
+**Alternative**: keep two builders split by repo shape: `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 for docs-first repos, `session-coherence-skill-generator` for every other shape and for young repos, each named in the front door's routing.
+**Impact if accepted**: `INTENT.md` lifecycle, `README.md` "How to use this repo", `entropy-assessment` Steps 3 and 4d, `docs-first-planning-assessment` Phase 2 and `guards-integrator` "When to Run" change to match. Either way, one place says which skill builds guards for which shape.
+
+---
+
+### Proposed: one statement of the next validation loop
+
+**Status**: Proposed on 2026-10-07 by an entropy assessment. Awaiting Justin Philpott's decision; not in force.
+**Context**: "Farm broader entropic-immunity exploration…" below sets the loop as assessing "a larger set of open source projects" and tracking "whether that produces more merged PRs". `INTENT.md` ("Scope boundary and next validation loop") sets it on docs-first planning repos and tracks clearer session recovery, fewer reintroduced stale ideas, more coherent docs and sharper feedback. `README.md` "Project status" and `TODO.md` "Next Up" follow `INTENT.md`.
+**Proposal**: `INTENT.md` holds the one statement of the loop and measures both: merged changes where the target is an external open-source repo, and session-recovery quality everywhere. The other files link to it.
+**Alternative**: the decision entry's wording (open-source repos, merged PRs) governs, and `INTENT.md` is corrected to it.
+**Impact if accepted**: `INTENT.md` gains one sentence; `README.md` "Project status" and `TODO.md` "Next Up" link to it rather than restate it.
